  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Practice and the Dojo. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 9: Andrea Magnorsky from SCNA 2012 (2012).",
  "Andrea brought an international perspective to SCNA Chicago, showing how the Alt.NET ethos spread across Europe.",
  "Who inspired Andrea to look beyond conventional business applications toward game development and functional programming? How did European and American developer communities cross-pollinate? What principles guided Andrea Magnorsky when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: NaFFbjd9umM). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Siloed engineering leads to stagnation. Modern AI toolchains require cross-disciplinary curiosity across graphics, functional paradigms, and distributed data. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 10. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
